# Testing

**Unit tests** live beside their code (`src/core/resolve.test.ts`). The `law`
job runs them and they are **always green**. They are yours — write as many as
you like.

**Acceptance tests** (`tests/acceptance/`) are the **scoreboard**. They are
red until their card lands, and they are **never a merge gate** — `npm run law`
does not run them; `npm run progress` reports them.

They are authored *ahead* of the card they define. You may not edit, skip,
weaken, retitle or delete one. Not to make it match your implementation, not
to fix a typo.

If an acceptance test looks wrong, **bounce** (AGENTS.md) — open a card
question rather than a guess. A card that edits its own definition of done has
proven nothing, and `task-lint` fails any diff touching `tests/acceptance/`.

This has already earned its keep twice: an agent found a genuinely
self-contradictory acceptance test and refused to proceed, and three agents in
a row refused to relax a unit test that blocked them and reported the scoping
error instead.
